  {
   "line": 5,
   "text": "The recipe that does it is the bilinear transform. Near zero, the ruler lands almost one for one: five hundred hertz lands on four ninety-four. Further up it squeezes harder, and infinity lands exactly on four thousand. That uneven squeeze is warping. And thirty-four hundred lands on twenty-three sixty-three. There's your bug, in one row.",
